---
// Reader: a programme or service owner choosing where AI could help their team.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import { describeServiceHref } from '../../data/contact';
import { teamRecordFull } from '../../data/team';
const context = 'AI-assisted public services';
---
<Base title="AI for public services | Registry Stack" description="Design a service, adapt its rules or let people prepare requests with an approved assistant. Explore three uses of AI, with review and approval by your institution." ogImagePath="/og-ai.png" ogImageAlt="Registry Stack: Design, adapt and access public services with AI.">
  <SiteHeader current="ai" />
  <main id="main-content" tabindex="-1">
    <section class="hero hero-cover" aria-labelledby="ai-title"><div class="hero-inner"><div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">AI for public services</p>
      <h1 id="ai-title">Design, adapt and access public services with AI.</h1>
      <p class="hero-lead">Use AI to help define a service, prepare implementation changes or help people make a request. Your institution approves the rules and the changes to its service.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions"><a class="button button-primary" href={describeServiceHref(context)} data-journey="service-inquiry">Discuss your service</a><a class="button button-secondary" href="#uses">Explore the three uses</a></div>
    </div></div></section>

    <section class="section" id="uses" aria-labelledby="uses-title"><div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-heading"><h2 id="uses-title">Where would AI help your service?</h2></div>
      <div class="ai-paths">
        <article><p class="eyebrow">Service design</p><h3>Prepare a brief and test a prototype</h3><p>Use research, forms and procedures to work through the service with staff and applicants. Give your delivery team a reviewed brief.</p><p class="path-status">A scoped engagement, mainly through our partners.</p><a class="inline-cta" href="/ai/service-design/">Explore service design <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article>
        <article><p class="eyebrow">Implementation</p><h3>Adapt a service to your rules</h3><p>Our team uses AI to draft configuration, test cases and guidance. We check the drafts; your team approves the changes before release.</p><p class="path-status">A paid implementation pilot with Aubex.</p><a class="inline-cta" href="/customization/">See how implementation works <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article>
        <article id="citizen-access"><p class="eyebrow">Citizen access</p><h3>Help people prepare a request</h3><p>An assistant you approve reads the details you allow and prepares a draft. The person checks and submits it on your official website. The assistant cannot submit, approve or change a record.</p><p class="path-status">Available in a pilot for a configured Base Registry Engine service.</p><a class="inline-cta" href="/ai/citizen-access/">See the citizen access example <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article>
      </div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="section section-muted" aria-labelledby="control-title"><div class="section-inner approach-split">
      <div class="section-heading"><h2 id="control-title">Your team sets the rules.</h2><p>AI can propose a design or draft a change. Your institution confirms the service rules, and reviews and approves implementation changes.</p><p>The configured registry service runs without an AI model. For citizen access, you choose which assistants may connect and what they can read and prepare.</p><a class="inline-cta" href="/architecture/headless/">How it fits your existing systems <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
      <div class="editorial-callout"><p class="eyebrow">Authoring tool · In development</p><h3>Registry Studio</h3><p>A workspace for reviewing records, service steps and proposed changes with your technical team. Its local prototype also uses existing documents to prepare a draft brief for review.</p><a class="inline-cta" href="/products/studio/">Explore Registry Studio <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="team-title"><div class="section-inner approach-split">
      <div class="section-heading"><h2 id="team-title">Built on ten years of registry work</h2><p>{teamRecordFull}</p><p>The core runtime software is Apache-2.0 open source. Your institution can inspect, adapt and operate it with its own team or another provider. Aubex offers paid implementation and support.</p></div>
      <div class="editorial-callout"><h3>Inspect the software and its boundaries</h3><ul class="check-links"><li><a href="https://github.com/registrystack/registry-stack">Source code and releases</a></li><li><a href="https://docs.registrystack.org/security/#an-ai-assistant-acting-for-a-citizen">Security model for citizen assistants</a></li><li><a href="/pricing/">Implementation and support options</a></li></ul></div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="final-cta" aria-labelledby="next-title"><div class="section-inner"><h2 id="next-title">Start with one service.</h2><p>Bring a form, a process or a request people make often. We’ll agree what to evaluate, who reviews it and what your team receives.</p><div class="section-links"><a class="button button-primary" href={describeServiceHref(context)} data-journey="service-inquiry">Discuss your service</a><a class="button button-secondary" href="/pricing/">View implementation options</a></div></div></section>
  </main><SiteFooter />
</Base>
<style>
  .ai-paths { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: clamp(24px, 4vw, 48px); }
  .ai-paths article { border-top: 2px solid var(--registry-blue); display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: start; padding-top: 24px; }
  .ai-paths h3 { font-size: var(--type-xl); }
  .ai-paths .path-status { font-size: var(--type-sm); }
  .ai-paths .inline-cta { margin-top: auto; }
  .check-links { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  .check-links li { border-top: 1px solid var(--registry-rule); padding: 14px 0; }
  @media (max-width: 820px) { .ai-paths { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
